# Rung 5a, host A: the standing reader service, fed from the LABELED path.
#
# Identical to fed-reader-service-web.actions except for the turn script, which reads
# the same page from /untrusted instead of over HTTP. Rung 2's --ladder-untrusted-paths
# is what gives that mount meaning, so this is the run where the reader's sentry sets
# the taint bit and every later stamp this service writes carries taint=1.
#
# --max-exchanges is 2 here rather than 3, and the difference is the whole recycle
# demonstration. The service takes the untrusted read on its first exchange and is
# tainted from that moment; the second exchange is served by a tainted service, and the
# federation proxy -- which sees taint=1 in the stamp on the way past, and does not have
# to ask anyone -- requests the recycle. Two exchanges is the residual window, stated as
# a number the demo prints rather than as a caveat in prose.

serve-agent --max-exchanges 2 --idle-timeout 40 --on-message /ladder/probes/fed-reader-turn-labeled.actions
